00:07:31.880 --> 00:07:35.240
It's kind of discovering
again your systems,

00:07:35.240 --> 00:07:39.320
going through inventory of
each server that you have,

00:07:39.320 --> 00:07:41.330
each network that
you have set up.

00:07:41.330 --> 00:07:43.580
How do applications
talk to each other?

00:07:43.580 --> 00:07:45.980
Where do you have
load balancing set up?

00:07:45.980 --> 00:07:47.390
Where is the caching?

00:07:47.390 --> 00:07:49.830
And what is the
security set up like?

00:07:49.830 --> 00:07:51.650
What can talk to each other?

00:07:51.650 --> 00:07:52.550
What can't?

00:07:52.550 --> 00:07:56.060
This was so critical for
us that without this I

00:07:56.060 --> 00:07:57.942
don't think we would
have been successful.

00:07:57.942 --> 00:07:59.900
WILLIAM ANDERSON: And
