00:08:25.730 --> 00:08:29.360
Right now we had new kind
of diagrams of data diagrams

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:33.270
and architecture kind of
plans of how everything works.

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:36.140
So we could actually walk
our partners through it,

00:08:36.140 --> 00:08:38.780
and show them how
everything is set up.

00:08:38.780 --> 00:08:43.250
So our kind of onboarding of our
partner was made a lot easier

00:08:43.250 --> 00:08:46.970
by us doing that
prep work prior.

00:08:46.970 --> 00:08:50.030
So next step was
planning the architecture

00:08:50.030 --> 00:08:53.130
and figuring out how it's
going to look in the Cloud.

00:08:53.130 --> 00:08:56.060
So we have our
architecture on prem,

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:58.663
and then how do we
move it to the Cloud?

00:08:58.663 --> 00:09:00.830
And that went through a lot
of different iterations,

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:04.650
to be honest, and until
we were happy with it.

00:09:04.650 --> 00:09:07.970
So that was a step that
was also critical for us.

00:09:07.970 --> 00:09:10.140
Then the kickoff, which
was very exciting.

00:09:10.140 --> 00:09:13.080
We wanted to move forward
as soon as possible.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:15.590
And we started migrating.

00:09:15.590 --> 00:09:18.200
At some point, obviously,
we realized that we

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.640
should do things different.

00:09:19.640 --> 00:09:23.820
So that took some time
for us to get comfortable.

00:09:23.820 --> 00:09:26.330
But we were very happy
to get everything first

00:09:26.330 --> 00:09:30.560
to the development
project, and then

00:09:30.560 --> 00:09:32.780
move everything to
staging, and then start

00:09:32.780 --> 00:09:34.790
moving into production.

00:09:34.790 --> 00:09:38.490
Our approach was to move
to production in phases.

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:41.990
And it was a good
approach, and mostly we

00:09:41.990 --> 00:09:43.360
