00:31:26.980 --> 00:31:30.010
new instances, and migrate
those between dev state

00:31:30.010 --> 00:31:30.900
and production.

00:31:30.900 --> 00:31:34.110
But we can set up an entirely
new ecosystem on the fly

00:31:34.110 --> 00:31:34.693
as we need to.

00:31:34.693 --> 00:31:36.693
VADIM SUPITSKIY: And we
already started on that,

00:31:36.693 --> 00:31:38.890
and right now as we kind
of discussed and mentioned,

00:31:38.890 --> 00:31:41.760
we can create an
application cluster

00:31:41.760 --> 00:31:43.570
anything in that environment.

00:31:43.570 --> 00:31:45.900
But we want to be able to
with one push of a button

00:31:45.900 --> 00:31:48.670
to generate everything
right away anywhere.

00:31:48.670 --> 00:31:49.170
Right?

00:31:49.170 --> 00:31:52.390
So this is going to be a huge
step for us in the future.

00:31:52.390 --> 00:31:55.160
And I think that's pretty
much the next step for us.

00:31:55.160 --> 00:31:56.910
WILLIAM ANDERSON: Which
